      "updated": 1785261806979,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "ch03 data engineering fundamentals\n    - data sources (analytical, transactional) -> ETL/ELT -> feature engineering -> model training, development, evaluation -> deployment\n        - data sources can be logs, user data, third party; just be mindful of inherent bias with certain data & features\n    - batch vs streaming processing\n    - data formats\n        - agnostic: JSON, CSV, yaml, xml\n        - specific: pickle, protobuf, parquet\n\n    - more about data bases (Thomas to make a dedicated frame on databases)\n        - \n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "ch03 data engineering fundamentals\n    - data sources (analytical, transactional) -> ETL/ELT -> feature engineering -> model training, development, evaluation -> deployment\n        - data sources can be logs, user data, third party; just be mindful of inherent bias with certain data & features\n    - batch vs streaming processing\n    - data formats\n        - agnostic: JSON, CSV, yaml, xml\n        - specific: pickle, protobuf, parquet\n\n    - more about data bases (Thomas to make a dedicated frame on databases)\n        - \n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ksqFTlPKd6zLRRP6zL6Gq",
      "type": "text",
